>3. I find that the character classes in Nethack don't have much distinction
>between them... unless i'm missing something of course... could someone out
>there outline the character classes in Nethack? Thanx.
 You are missing a lot - have you actually played Netahack or just watched
over someones shoulder? 
 
 Priests come with the useful ability of knowing whether and item is
cursed or bless or regular. Barbarians have little magical ability but are
powerful fighters and come with poison resistance. Samurai are good
fighters and have the dungeon feature more oriental objects than normal.
Valkyrie are the only females to choose and have cold resistance.
Archaologists (sp) come armed with bullwhip and wearing a fedora and
leather jacket, they can tell what a gem is and come with tools to mine
and can food. Thieves are pretty useless - they come with a potion of
sickness to poison darts. Knights come heavily armoured. Cavemen are
stupid and come with a club to bash monsters with. Wizards come with
various magical items and a cloak of magic resistance - can't fight for
nuts though. Elves have heaps of useful intrinsics to star with.
 
 Basically each class has different intrinsics and equiptment to differ
them as well as magical and fighting ability.

